{
  "_comment": "The Xbox 360 remote's face, which its guide shows only as a photo: the 555's guide drawing (page 5, tools/remote_art.py) rearranged to the Xbox 360 as photographed - its round keys print no words under them, Menu and Info's bar gives way to the Y, X, A and B keys (Guide under Y, Live TV under B), Exit shares its bar with Menu, Back and Info take the 555's Sound and Picture keys, the number pad's corners print * . and # input, and the bottom row is clear, display, title and enter (`source.erase`, and `source.marks` for what is new). Every key is a key: the Xbox 360 is the 525/555 key grid relabelled, so a key takes the scan of the key in its place on the 555 (Y the Guide key, B Info, Back and Info Sound and Picture, the bottom row the colour keys). Widened by 1.1 and its case painted white as the 555's.",
